  "summary": "Ilkal sari or Ilkal seere is a traditional form of sari which is a common feminine wear in India.",
  "description": "Ilkal sari or Ilkal seere is a traditional form of sari which is a common feminine wear in India. Ilkal sari takes its name from the town of Ilkal in the Bagalkot district of Karnataka state, India. Ilkal saris are woven using cotton warp on the body and art silk warp for border and art silk warp for pallu portion of the sari. In some cases instead of art silk, pure silk is also used.",
  "culturalContext": "Registered as a Geographical Indication of India (handicraft, Karnataka; registration 2007–08), which protects the name for products made in its place of origin by traditional methods.",
